  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: The current best (config_037, 0.706 acc) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l in a multimodal setting. We know scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 in the multimodal context (0.678 vs 0.639 with resnet50), but we cannot yet tell how much of that gain comes from the RNA encoder itself versus an interaction with the image modality. The RNA-only multiprofile avgpool baseline with pca is 0.591 (config_002), but we have no RNA-only scvi_n200 counterpart. 2) What this tests: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder relative to config_002. It directly quantifies the isolated contribution of scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000 without the confound of image features or fusion. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: The answer strategically redirects the remaining budget. If scvi alone reaches ~0.65+, the image modality adds little and further gains should come from RNA-side improvements (e.g., scgpt). If scvi alone stays near ~0.60, the multimodal combination is essential and we should exploit the image/fusion dimensions (e.g., transformer aggregation in config_039, or scgpt in the multimodal setting). This single experiment resolves a key uncertainty that no other available configuration addresses as cleanly, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

